        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Retrieves the node representing &quot;once &apos;part&apos;s own ``run =`` call (if it makes one) has
returned&quot; :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

For a part that makes no call, this is just ``{part, false}`` -- there&apos;s no call to
distinguish &quot;before&quot; from &quot;after&quot;, so the part&apos;s own node already serves both purposes
</verbatim></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>part</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The part to look up </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Either <computeroutput>{part, true}</computeroutput> (if the part makes a <computeroutput>run =</computeroutput> call) or <computeroutput>{part, false}</computeroutput> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
